# Findings that are understood and not acted on. Each names the reason; an
# entry without one is how a suppression file becomes a way of not looking.

# DS-0002 — no USER in Containerfile.dev.
#
# It is a development image. It is never deployed, it runs on a developer's own
# machine with their checkout bind-mounted in, and everything it exists to do —
# installing toolchains, building, running linters against a bind mount owned
# by the host user — is what a non-root user would break. The service image
# beside it, Containerfile.git, does drop privilege, because that one listens
# on a socket.
DS-0002
